cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OS Tutor in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OS Tutor: A Fine-Tuned, Retrieval-Grounded and Simulator-Verified Tutor for Operating Systems"
type: software
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-24"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Divyakush2006/OS-Tutor"
authors:
  - family-names: Punjabi
    given-names: Divyakush
    affiliation: "School of Computer Science and Engineering (SCOPE), Vellore Institute of Technology"
abstract: >-
  OS Tutor is a locally hosted teaching system for undergraduate Operating Systems. A fine-tuned
  4B-parameter model explains concepts and teaches Socratically, while verified simulators compute
  every numerical answer, hybrid retrieval grounds explanations in cited sources, and code checks
  every reply before it is shown.
keywords:
  - operating systems education
  - intelligent tutoring system
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - QLoRA
  - tool-augmented reasoning
